## Phase 2 — Google sign-in

Google Identity Services, ID-token flow — no client secret, no redirect route.

- **Migration** (needs Phase 0): `users.hashed_password` → nullable; add `auth_provider`, `google_sub` (unique, indexed), `email_verified`. `avatar_url` already exists at `models/__init__.py:66` and is already in `UserResponse` — wire Google's `picture` claim into it.
- **Guard `login`**: `auth.py:70` calls `verify_password(payload.password, user.hashed_password)` unguarded. With nullable hashes that crashes. A Google-only account attempting password login must get a clean 400 telling them to use Google.
- **Rewrite `POST /auth/oauth/callback`** (`auth.py:114-129`) — currently a stub returning tokens for hardcoded UUID `00000000-...-0001`, which isn't in the database, so those tokens 401 on the very next request. Replace with: verify the ID token signature against Google's JWKS, check `aud`/`iss`/`exp`, then look-up-or-create the user by `google_sub` and issue your own JWTs. Add `google-auth` to `requirements.txt`; there is currently no OAuth library of any kind.
- **Account linking:** decide whether a Google sign-in whose email matches an existing password account links to it or is rejected. Auto-linking on unverified email is a real account-takeover vector — only link when Google reports `email_verified`.
- **Frontend:** the button already exists at `LoginForm.tsx:60-62`, permanently `disabled` with `title="OAuth placeholder"`. Wire it up, add `auth.google()` to `lib/api.ts` (no OAuth client function exists), add `NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID`, and mirror it onto `RegisterForm`.

Worth folding in while here: the refresh token is stored in `localStorage` but `POST /auth/refresh` is **never called** from the frontend, so every session hard-expires after 30 minutes with a raw error string. Add refresh-on-401 to `apiFetch` (`lib/api.ts:54-69`).

