## Parked — cost & billing

Deferred at your request. The raw material gets captured in Phase 1c regardless (the `usage` object is currently discarded), so nothing is lost by deciding later. When you're ready, the scoping questions are: per-call token/cost persistence and a usage dashboard; a monthly spend cap with auto-fallback; Redis caching of AI results to avoid re-billing repeat analyses; and Railway hosting-cost tuning.

One thing worth deciding early: `services/cache.py` swallows **every** exception, so if you later build a Redis-backed spend cap, it fails *open* — silently becoming a no-op exactly when a cost runaway is most likely.

